Subject: [PATCH] =?UTF-8?q?feat(kit):=20atajos=20con=20NamedKey=20y=20que?=
 =?UTF-8?q?=20no=20lleguen=20tambi=C3=A9n=20como=20tecla?=
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

ShortcutKey::Named admite flechas, teclas de función y de edición. Un atajo
que dispara su acción ya no se reenvía a la app. Lo pide CurseTerm (BK-003):
un terminal no debe recibir la tecla de un atajo del menú.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01F89v1xFeQ2WCVD25PBsobh
---
 crates/barrier-kit/src/app/action.rs          | 12 ++++++++++++
 crates/barrier-kit/src/platform/input/seat.rs |  3 ++-
 docs/barrierkit/11-app.en.md                  |  4 ++--
 docs/barrierkit/11-app.md                     |  4 ++--
 4 files changed, 18 insertions(+), 5 deletions(-)

diff --git a/crates/barrier-kit/src/app/action.rs b/crates/barrier-kit/src/app/action.rs
index 387483d..afae01e 100644
--- a/crates/barrier-kit/src/app/action.rs
+++ b/crates/barrier-kit/src/app/action.rs
@@ -10,6 +10,7 @@ pub enum ShortcutKey {
     Char(char),
     Left,
     Right,
+    Named(NamedKey),
 }
 
 #[derive(Clone, Copy, Debug, PartialEq, Eq)]
@@ -34,6 +35,7 @@ impl Shortcut {
             }
             (ShortcutKey::Left, Key::Named(NamedKey::ArrowLeft))
             | (ShortcutKey::Right, Key::Named(NamedKey::ArrowRight)) => true,
+            (ShortcutKey::Named(named), Key::Named(pressed)) => named == *pressed,
             _ => false,
         };
         same_key && modifiers == self.modifiers
@@ -55,6 +57,7 @@ impl Shortcut {
             ShortcutKey::Char(c) => c.to_uppercase().to_string(),
             ShortcutKey::Left => "Left".into(),
             ShortcutKey::Right => "Right".into(),
+            ShortcutKey::Named(named) => named.to_string(),
         });
         parts.join("+")
     }
@@ -208,11 +211,20 @@ mod tests {
                 Modifiers::CONTROL | Modifiers::SHIFT,
                 ShortcutKey::Char('z'),
             ),
+            Shortcut::new(
+                Modifiers::META | Modifiers::ALT,
+                ShortcutKey::Named(NamedKey::ArrowUp),
+            ),
+            Shortcut::new(Modifiers::empty(), ShortcutKey::Named(NamedKey::F11)),
+            Shortcut::new(Modifiers::SHIFT, ShortcutKey::Named(NamedKey::PageDown)),
         ];
         let keys = [
             Key::Character("n".into()),
             Key::Named(NamedKey::ArrowLeft),
             Key::Character("z".into()),
+            Key::Named(NamedKey::ArrowUp),
+            Key::Named(NamedKey::F11),
+            Key::Named(NamedKey::PageDown),
         ];
         for (shortcut, key) in shortcuts.iter().zip(&keys) {
             assert!(shortcut.matches(shortcut.modifiers, key));
diff --git a/crates/barrier-kit/src/platform/input/seat.rs b/crates/barrier-kit/src/platform/input/seat.rs
index 976bf12..2a99851 100644
--- a/crates/barrier-kit/src/platform/input/seat.rs
+++ b/crates/barrier-kit/src/platform/input/seat.rs
@@ -461,10 +461,11 @@ impl Runtime {
             modifiers,
         };
         if let Some(idx) = index {
-            self.surfaces[idx].app.push(platform_event);
             if shortcut_action.is_some() {
                 self.poll_all();
                 self.redraw_all();
+            } else {
+                self.surfaces[idx].app.push(platform_event);
             }
         }
     }
diff --git a/docs/barrierkit/11-app.en.md b/docs/barrierkit/11-app.en.md
index a4b79f0..44293ab 100644
--- a/docs/barrierkit/11-app.en.md
+++ b/docs/barrierkit/11-app.en.md
@@ -23,11 +23,11 @@ use_menu_action(move |id| {
 ```
 
 - `Shortcut::new(modificadores, tecla)` or `Shortcut::ctrl(tecla)`; the keys
-  are `ShortcutKey::Char(c)`, `Left` and `Right`.
+  are `ShortcutKey::Char(c)`, `Left`, `Right` and `Named(NamedKey)` (`ArrowUp`, `F11`, `PageDown`…).
 - `RESET.item(true)` creates the menu entry; `item_with(true, CheckState::Checkbox(on))`
   creates it with a checkbox.
 - The handler always runs on the interface thread.
-- A shortcut only arrives if its action is in the window's menu.
+- A shortcut only arrives if its action is in the window's menu. When it fires its action, the key no longer reaches the app.
 
 | Kit action | Shortcut |
 |---|---|
diff --git a/docs/barrierkit/11-app.md b/docs/barrierkit/11-app.md
index 5ca5e64..1c53334 100644
--- a/docs/barrierkit/11-app.md
+++ b/docs/barrierkit/11-app.md
@@ -24,11 +24,11 @@ use_menu_action(move |id| {
 ```
 
 - `Shortcut::new(modificadores, tecla)` o `Shortcut::ctrl(tecla)`; las teclas
-  son `ShortcutKey::Char(c)`, `Left` y `Right`.
+  son `ShortcutKey::Char(c)`, `Left`, `Right` y `Named(NamedKey)` (`ArrowUp`, `F11`, `PageDown`…).
 - `RESET.item(true)` crea la entrada del menú; `item_with(true, CheckState::Checkbox(on))`
   la crea con casilla.
 - El handler corre siempre en el hilo de la interfaz.
-- Un atajo solo llega si su acción está en el menú de la ventana.
+- Un atajo solo llega si su acción está en el menú de la ventana. Cuando dispara su acción, la tecla ya no llega a la app.
 
 | Acción del kit | Atajo |
 |---|---|
